IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei6-part-8-4-administration`

-- Tests of ei6-part-8-4-administration (Act ss 153.12 to 153.14, src:2879-2965). Expected values are read from the
-- text by hand. In every adaptation the first argument is "the adaptation has not ceased to apply under section 153.14".

§ `Section 153.14 - cessation of effect`

#ASSERT `s 153.14 the latest day on which a provision added by an Interim Order may cease to apply` EQUALS YMD 2027 6 2
-- no repeal: the provision ceases on June 2, 2027, and applies through that day (fork F-ei6-7).
#ASSERT `s 153.14 the day on which the provision ceases to apply` NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2027 6 2
#ASSERT `s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` (YMD 2027 6 2) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` (YMD 2027 6 3) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) NOTHING
-- an Interim Order repealed earlier ends it earlier; one repealed later does not extend it.
#ASSERT `s 153.14 the day on which the provision ceases to apply` (JUST (YMD 2021 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2021 3 1
#ASSERT `s 153.14 the day on which the provision ceases to apply` (JUST (YMD 2028 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2027 6 2
#ASSERT `s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` (YMD 2021 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2021 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.14 the provision still applies on the day` (YMD 2021 3 2) (JUST (YMD 2021 3 1)))

§ `Section 153.12 - the Social Insurance Number`

#ASSERT `s 153.12 the Minister may collect and use the Social Insurance Number of the claimant` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.12 the Minister may collect and use the Social Insurance Number of the claimant` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.12 the Minister may collect and use the Social Insurance Number of the claimant` TRUE FALSE)

§ `Sections 153.121 and 153.13 - the benefit period`

-- (1): a benefit period established before March 15, 2020 ends the day before the first week for which the benefit is paid.
-- Sunday April 5, 2020 begins the first week paid, so the benefit period ends on Saturday April 4, 2020 (src:2883).
#ASSERT `s 153.121(1) the last day of the benefit period` (YMD 2020 1 5) (YMD 2020 4 5) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 4 4)
#ASSERT `s 153.121(1) the last day of the benefit period` (YMD 2020 3 14) (YMD 2020 3 15) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 3 14)
-- a benefit period beginning on March 15, 2020 or later is not one this subsection ends.
#ASSERT `s 153.121(1) the last day of the benefit period` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 4 5) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): after reconsideration a benefit period beginning before March 15, 2020 does not end (src:2885).
#ASSERT `s 153.121(1) the last day of the benefit period` (YMD 2020 1 5) (YMD 2020 4 5) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.121(2) the benefit period does not end and the claimant is deemed not to have been eligible by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.121(2) the benefit period does not end and the claimant is deemed not to have been eligible by reason of paragraph 153.9(2)(a)` FALSE)
-- 153.13: the weeks during which the benefit was paid are not taken into account (src:2887). Weeks by the date of their Sunday.
#ASSERT `s 153.13 the weeks taken into account in establishing the benefit period` (LIST YMD 2020 3 1, YMD 2020 3 8, YMD 2020 3 15, YMD 2020 3 22) (LIST YMD 2020 3 15, YMD 2020 3 22) EQUALS LIST YMD 2020 3 1, YMD 2020 3 8
#ASSERT null (`s 153.13 the weeks taken into account in establishing the benefit period` (LIST YMD 2020 3 15) (LIST YMD 2020 3 15))

§ `Section 153.1301 - section 44 as adapted`

#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the person must return the amount without delay` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the person must return the amount without delay` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the person must return the amount without delay` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the person must return the amount without delay` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- the whole payment if not eligible; the excess if eligible for less; nothing to return otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned` TRUE FALSE 1000 0 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned` TRUE TRUE 1500 1000 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned` TRUE TRUE 1000 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned` TRUE TRUE 800 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1301 as adapted s 44 the amount to be returned` FALSE FALSE 1000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 153.1302 and 153.1303 - sections 50 and 52 as adapted`

-- 50(1): not eligible until the information is provided, or the claimant complies with the requirement to attend.
#ASSERT `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(1) the claimant is not eligible until they provide the information or comply` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(2) the Commission may require the claimant to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1302 as adapted s 50(2) the Commission may require the claimant to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` TRUE FALSE)
-- 52(2): the Commission must calculate and notify.
#ASSERT `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount and notify the claimant of its decision` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount and notify the claimant of its decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount and notify the claimant of its decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- 52(4): the amount calculated is payable if the Commission decides the person was eligible and the money was not paid.
#ASSERT `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE 750 EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` TRUE TRUE FALSE 750 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE 750 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1303 as adapted s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` FALSE TRUE TRUE 750 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 153.1305 - section 112 as adapted`

-- (1): within 30 days after the day the decision is communicated, or any further time the Commission allows (src:2904-2905).
-- The decision was communicated on June 1, 2020; the 30th day after is July 1, 2020 (fork F-ei6-10).
#ASSERT `s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 7 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 7 2) FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 8 15) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 5 31) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 6 10) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(1) as adapted s 112(1) the person may make a request for reconsideration` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 6 10) FALSE)
-- (2): the request is in writing and contains the particulars (src:2907-2908).
#ASSERT `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(4) the request for reconsideration is in the form required` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(5) the request for reconsideration is filed as required` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(5) the request for reconsideration is filed as required` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1305(2) as added s 112(5) the request for reconsideration is filed as required` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 153.1306 - write-off`

-- (1)(e): not the debtor's error or declaration, but a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount (src:2915-2917).
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1)(e) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or declaration but from a retrospective ruling or an excess weekly amount` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1)(f): the Commission considers (src:2918-2921).
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1)(f) the Commission considers that the amount is uncollectable or that collecting it would be unduly hard or costly` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1)(f) the Commission considers that the amount is uncollectable or that collecting it would be unduly hard or costly` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1)(f) the Commission considers that the amount is uncollectable or that collecting it would be unduly hard or costly` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1)(f) the Commission considers that the amount is uncollectable or that collecting it would be unduly hard or costly` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (1): any of (a) to (f). Arguments: not ceased; amount; deceased; discharged bankrupt; undischarged bankrupt; (e); (f).
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 100.01 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 5000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 5000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` TRUE 5000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(1) the Commission may write off the amount payable under section 43` FALSE 50 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (2): the portion of an amount owing under section 47 (src:2922-2929). Arguments: not ceased; debtor's error; false
-- declaration; (i) Commission delay; (ii) retrospective review; (iii) employer's record; (iv) employer's calculation; (v) insuring.
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1306(2) the Commission may write off the portion of the amount owing under section 47 received before notification` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Sections 153.1307 to 153.13091`

#ASSERT `s 153.1307 as adapted s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1307 as adapted s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE FALSE)
-- 126(1): an unpaid amount payable under Part I, II, VII.1 or VIII.4 (src:2935).
#ASSERT `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` TRUE `Part VIII.4` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` TRUE `Part I` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` TRUE `Part II` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` TRUE `Part VII.1` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` TRUE `Part VIII` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(1) the Commission may certify the unpaid amount` TRUE `Part VIII.4` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(2) the certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt of the amount specified` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1308 as adapted s 126(2) the certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt of the amount specified` TRUE FALSE)
-- 138: a Social Insurance Number for everyone employed in insurable employment and every self-employed person (src:2941).
#ASSERT `s 153.1309 as adapted s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1309 as adapted s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1309 as adapted s 138 the person must have a Social Insurance Number assigned under an Act of Parliament` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 153.13091 the Part that subsections 27(1) and (2) of the Regulations name for the emergency response benefit` EQUALS `Part VIII.4`

§ `Section 153.1310 - special rules`

#ASSERT `s 153.1310 the special rules apply to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 153.1310 the special rules apply to the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1310 the special rules apply to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1310 the special rules apply to the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(a) the person is deemed to have made a claim for the emergency response benefit under section 153.8` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1310(a) the person is deemed to have made a claim for the emergency response benefit under section 153.8` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 153.1310(b) the person must make the claim in accordance with subsection 153.8(1)` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(b) the person must make the claim in accordance with subsection 153.8(1)` FALSE
-- (c)(i): the difference between $500 and the benefits received for the week; (c)(ii): above $500 is deemed to be $500.
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(i) the amount of the emergency response benefit to be paid for the week` TRUE 300 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(i) the amount of the emergency response benefit to be paid for the week` TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(i) the amount of the emergency response benefit to be paid for the week` TRUE 600 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(i) the amount of the emergency response benefit to be paid for the week` FALSE 300 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week, as deemed` TRUE 300 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week, as deemed` TRUE 600 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week, as deemed` FALSE 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week to which section 44 does not apply` TRUE 600 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week to which section 44 does not apply` TRUE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 153.1310(c)(ii) the amount of benefits received for the week to which section 44 does not apply` FALSE 600 EQUALS NOTHING
